### Algorithm 2: Riemannian Barycenter Computation

```
ALGORITHM 2: RiemannianBarycentre({y_i}, {w_i}, ε_fuse, k_max)

INPUT:  Points {y_i} ⊂ S^{d-1}, weights {w_i} with Σw_i = 1
        Convergence threshold ε_fuse, maximum iterations k_max
OUTPUT: Fréchet mean ȳ ∈ S^{d-1}

─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1.  ȳ ← y_{argmax_i w_i}                   [initialize at highest-weight point]
2.  FOR k = 0, 1, 2, ..., k_max:
3.      grad ← Σ_i w_i · Log(ȳ, y_i)       [weighted sum of log maps]
            where Log(y, z) = arccos(⟨y,z⟩) / √(1-⟨y,z⟩²) · (z - ⟨y,z⟩·y)
4.      ȳ_new ← Exp(ȳ, grad)               [exponential map step]
            where Exp(y, v) = cos(‖v‖)·y + sin(‖v‖)·v/‖v‖
5.      IF d_g(ȳ_new, ȳ) < ε_fuse:         [convergence check]
6.          RETURN ȳ_new
7.      ȳ ← ȳ_new
8.  LOG "Barycenter did not converge in k_max iterations"
9.  RETURN ȳ                                [best iterate as fallback]

─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
COMPLEXITY: O(k_max · N · d) per call
CONVERGENCE RATE: Linear with rate proportional to w_max
```

