### Algorithm 6: Gram Matrix Completeness Certification (Lemma 0)

```
ALGORITHM 6: CertifyCompleteness(B, ε₀, Δ_min)

INPUT:  Prototype matrix B ∈ R^{K×d} (rows are normalized prototypes)
        Completeness threshold ε₀, minimum diversity Δ_min
OUTPUT: CERTIFIED or INCOMPLETE with diagnostic

─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1.  G ← B · B^T                             [Gram matrix, K×K]
2.  FOR k = 1 to K:
3.      R_k ← Σ_{j≠k} |G[k,j]|             [Gershgorin radius]
4.      IF R_k ≥ G[k,k]:
5.          RETURN INCOMPLETE, reason="Gershgorin condition violated at type k"
6.  eigenvalues ← ComputeEigenvalues(G)
7.  IF min(eigenvalues) ≤ 0:
8.      RETURN INCOMPLETE, reason="Gram matrix not positive definite"
9.  dual_basis ← Inverse(G) · B             [dual basis vectors, K×d]
10. reconstruction_errors ← []
11. FOR k = 1 to K:
12.     FOR x in SampleTasks(T_k, n=100):
13.         x_embed ← Embed(x)
14.         x_recon ← Σ_j ⟨x_embed, B[j,:]⟩ · dual_basis[j,:]
15.         err ← ‖x_embed - x_recon‖
16.         reconstruction_errors.append(err)
17. ε̂₀ ← mean(reconstruction_errors)
18. IF ε̂₀ > ε₀:
19.     RETURN INCOMPLETE, reason=f"Reconstruction error {ε̂₀} > threshold {ε₀}"
20. Δ̂ ← 1 - max_{k≠j} |G[k,j]|
21. IF Δ̂ < Δ_min:
22.     RETURN INCOMPLETE, reason=f"Insufficient diversity Δ̂ = {Δ̂}"
23. RETURN CERTIFIED, {G: G, dual_basis: dual_basis, ε̂₀: ε̂₀, Δ̂: Δ̂}

─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
COMPLEXITY: O(K²d) for Gram construction, O(K³) for eigenvalues
DIAGNOSTIC: Failed certification identifies which task type violates
            coverage, guiding taxonomy extension.
```

