### Algorithm 9: Maakoul Efficiency Coefficient Computation (CTB-L)

```
ALGORITHM 9: ComputeEfficiencyCoefficient(x, y_out, E_actual, T_kelvin)

INPUT:  Task x, output y_out, actual energy E_actual (joules),
        Temperature T_kelvin (default 300K)
OUTPUT: Maakoul Efficiency Coefficient η_M, quality gap ΔR_k

─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1.  [Compute output entropy reduction]
2.  H_prior ← L · log2(V)                  [prior entropy: L tokens, vocab V]
3.  H_posterior ← -Σ_t Σ_v p(v|context_t) · log2(p(v|context_t))
                                            [actual output distribution entropy]
4.  ΔH ← H_prior - H_posterior             [entropy reduction in bits]

5.  [Landauer energy floor]
6.  k_B ← 1.380649e-23                     [Boltzmann constant, J/K]
7.  E_Landauer ← k_B · T_kelvin · ln(2) · ΔH
                                            [minimum energy in joules]

8.  [Maakoul Efficiency Coefficient]
9.  η_M ← E_Landauer / E_actual            [dimensionless, ∈ (0,1]]
    [Expected range: η_M ∼ 10^{-17} for silicon hardware]

10. [Rate-distortion quality gap (Lemma 7.1)]
11. D_actual ← DistortionEstimate(y_out, x) [task-specific distortion metric]
    D_optimal ← RateDistortionOptimalD(task_type, quality_target)
    ΔR_k ← RateDistortionFunction(D_actual) - RateDistortionFunction(D_optimal)
    [ΔR_k ≥ 0: positive if suboptimal model was routed]

12. [Excess energy from suboptimal routing]
    ΔE_subopt ← k_B · T_kelvin · ln(2) · ΔR_k
    [This is the thermodynamic cost of routing error]

13. RETURN η_M, ΔR_k, ΔE_subopt, E_Landauer

─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
LOGGING FORMAT per task:
{η_M, ΔR_k, ΔE_subopt, E_actual, ΔH, task_type, model_id, timestamp}

AGGREGATION: η_M_mean = E[η_M] across tasks
             Routing policies ranked by η_M_mean
             Δη_M = η_M_mean(R*) - η_M_mean(R_baseline) > 0
             confirms thermodynamic routing benefit (Corollary 7.1)
