─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PHASE 2: ROUTING CALIBRATION (MROT-S)

5.  FOR each model i, task type k:
6.      n_cert ← BernsteinSampleThreshold(ε, δ, V_i, M=1, N, K)  [Alg. 7]
7.      Collect n_cert performance samples from task_corpus
8.      μ̂[i,k], σ̂²[i,k] ← OnlineMoments(samples)
9.  LOG f"MROT-S: CERTIFIED. Sample complexity n_cert = {n_cert}"
10. LOG f"Specialization efficiency: specialist n_eff / generalist n_eff
         = {V_specialist/V_generalist:.2f}"

─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PHASE 3: CVF-R CALIBRATION

11. FOR each task type k:
12.     μ̂_k ← EmpiricalMonotonicity(V_M, T_k, n_samples=10000) [Alg. 4]
13.     L̂_k ← EmpiricalLipschitz(V_M, T_k, n_samples=10000)     [Alg. 5]
14.     IF μ̂_k ≤ 0: WARN "Validator not monotone on T_k"
15.     q*_k ← √(1 - μ̂_k²/L̂_k² + r²)  [r = π/8 default]
16.     LOG f"CVF-R Task {k}: μ̂={μ̂_k:.4f}, L̂={L̂_k:.4f}, q*={q*_k:.4f}"
17.     IF q*_k ≥ 1: WARN "Contraction not certified for T_k; reduce r"

